/// Bandit.HTTPError: an error suitable for return as an HTTP status.
///
/// Raised for malformed requests, which never reach the handler; the
/// pipeline answers the mapped status with Connection: close. Beamtalk
/// exceptions hold no instance state and caught instances do not dispatch
/// custom methods, so each non-400 status is a subclass (a catch filter)
/// and the pipeline maps via statusForClassName:.
typed Error subclass: HTTPError

  /// The response status for a caught error (Plug.Exception.status/1).
  /// Unknown subclasses default to 400, as Bandit's defexception does.
  /// If BT-4159 lands, these collapse to HTTPError signal:reason: with
  /// Integer reasons and the subclasses go away.
  class statusForClassName: name :: String -> Integer =>
    name match: [
      "HTTPError" -> 400;
      "HTTPError408" -> 408;
      "HTTPError414" -> 414;
      "HTTPError431" -> 431;
      _ -> 400
    ]
